 60FE c  {+60}Mn isotope obtained from the |b decay of {+60}Cr activity         
 60FE2c  which is produced by fragmentation of {+86}Kr beam                     
 60FE3c  at 140 MeV/nucleon hitting a {+9}Be target. The fragments              
 60FE4c  were separated by A1900 fragment separator. The fully-stripped         
 60FE5c  {+60}Cr ions were implanted in a double-sided Si detector              
 60FE6c  (DSSD) which was also a |b detector. Measured                          
 60FE7c  isotopic half-life, E|g, I|g, |g|g, |b|g coin. The |g                  
 60FE8c  rays were detected with a 12-detector segmented Ge detector array.     
 60FE9c  Comparisons with Shell-model calculations                              
 60FE cB IB,LOGFT$2006Li15 state that |b feeding intensities should be          
 60FE2cB considered as upper limits and associated apparent log| {Ift} values as
 60FE3cB lower limits                                                           
